WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.033
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to

00:00:02.033 --> 00:00:04.234
"The Tonight Show"!

00:00:04.234 --> 00:00:05.334
Thank you for watching.

00:00:05.334 --> 00:00:07.133
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:07.133 --> 00:00:08.167
Thank you for being here.

00:00:08.167 --> 00:00:09.501
Well, guys,
this is very exciting --

00:00:09.501 --> 00:00:11.968
after being canceled last year,
due to the pandemic,

00:00:11.968 --> 00:00:14.868
the New York City Marathon
is back this Sunday!

00:00:14.868 --> 00:00:18.934
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:00:18.934 --> 00:00:20.834
It's going to be a big day.
It's going to be a big day.

00:00:20.834 --> 00:00:23.300
At the starting line, runners
will take off their masks

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:25.434
and place them
over their nipples and --

00:00:25.434 --> 00:00:28.634
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.634 --> 00:00:30.000
My favorite part of the race is

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.334
when runners cross
the finish line.

00:00:31.334 --> 00:00:33.534
They immediately turn
into Chipotle burritos.

00:00:33.534 --> 00:00:35.400
[ Laughter and cheering ]

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:38.567
Of course,
the race is 26.2 miles

00:00:38.567 --> 00:00:40.734
and the only thing harder
than running a marathon

00:00:40.734 --> 00:00:43.033
is listening to someone
who just ran a marathon.

00:00:43.033 --> 00:00:45.067
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:47.033
Besides the marathon,
this Sunday is also

00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:48.634
daylight savings time.

00:00:48.634 --> 00:00:50.300
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:51.701
[ Booing ]

00:00:51.701 --> 00:00:54.267
The one thing Americans
can all agree on --

00:00:54.267 --> 00:00:55.968
hating daylight savings time.

00:00:55.968 --> 00:00:58.200
[ Laughter and applause ]
No one quite likes it, yeah.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:01.267
It's that magical trade where
we swap one extra hour of sleep

00:01:01.267 --> 00:01:03.400
for five months
of seasonal depression.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:04.467
I think that's nice.

00:01:04.467 --> 00:01:06.367
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:08.200
Seriously, what's more fun
than picking up your kids

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:09.801
from school in total darkness?

00:01:09.801 --> 00:01:10.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.868 --> 00:01:12.701
"Papa, is that you?"

00:01:12.701 --> 00:01:14.400
[ Whispering ]
Come closer to my voice.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:15.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.767 --> 00:01:17.534
Well, get this --
I saw that New York City

00:01:17.534 --> 00:01:20.767
has extended
its $100 vaccine incentive

00:01:20.767 --> 00:01:22.634
to kids ages 5 to 11.

00:01:22.634 --> 00:01:25.000
[ Oohs and cheering ]
A hundred bucks.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.868
Meanwhile, the smart kids
were like, "Yeah, make it $200,

00:01:26.868 --> 00:01:28.801
or we start doing
our own research."

00:01:28.801 --> 00:01:30.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:30.734 --> 00:01:32.434
Kind of sets a bad precedent.
I mean, every time you

00:01:32.434 --> 00:01:34.467
ask your kid to take medicine,
they're going to be like --

00:01:34.467 --> 00:01:35.534
[ New York accent ]
"You forgetting something, pal?"

00:01:35.534 --> 00:01:38.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.634 --> 00:01:40.267
That's right, after getting
the money, parents said,

00:01:40.267 --> 00:01:42.400
"Now, don't waste it."
And kids said,

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:44.634
"Oh, like how you bought
a $2,000 Peloton?"

00:01:44.634 --> 00:01:45.868
[ Laughter ]
Okay.

00:01:45.868 --> 00:01:48.701
I'm going to leave you
in the darkness.

00:01:48.701 --> 00:01:50.501
Some more COVID news --
today, Apple began

00:01:50.501 --> 00:01:54.868
dropping mask mandates
at some of its U.S. stores.

00:01:54.868 --> 00:01:56.901
Some think it's
because of the declining cases,

00:01:56.901 --> 00:01:58.267
but others say it's just
because Apple's

00:01:58.267 --> 00:02:00.367
about to release the iMask Pro.

00:02:00.367 --> 00:02:04.667
[ Laughter ]
[ Rimshot ]

00:02:04.667 --> 00:02:06.267
[ Applause ]
"That'll be $3,000."

00:02:06.267 --> 00:02:07.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.567 --> 00:02:10.334
But Apple says safety
is still their top priority.

00:02:10.334 --> 00:02:12.267
Then, they went back to letting
hundreds of strangers

00:02:12.267 --> 00:02:13.467
rub the same iPad.

00:02:13.467 --> 00:02:16.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.667 --> 00:02:18.133
[ Changes accent ]
"Ooh, this one looks nice!"

00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:20.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.634 --> 00:02:22.901
Don't lick it.

00:02:22.901 --> 00:02:25.634
Meanwhile, I saw that Uber's
bringing back UberPool,

00:02:25.634 --> 00:02:27.534
for the first time
since the pandemic began.

00:02:27.534 --> 00:02:29.000
[ Booing ]

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.567
It's great news,
if you love the bus,

00:02:30.567 --> 00:02:32.367
but dream of something
more intimate.

00:02:32.367 --> 00:02:34.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.234 --> 00:02:35.434
Some entertainment news --
today,

00:02:35.434 --> 00:02:37.968
Marvel's "Eternals"
finally hit theaters.

00:02:37.968 --> 00:02:40.934
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:02:43.033 --> 00:02:46.434
Marvel fans haven't been this
excited since two seconds ago,

00:02:46.434 --> 00:02:48.000
when the last Marvel movie
came out.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.434
"Eternals" is
about a young poet trying

00:02:51.434 --> 00:02:54.267
to find her voice
in postwar Europe.

00:02:54.267 --> 00:02:56.501
Just kidding. It's about
laser-shooting mutants.

00:02:56.501 --> 00:02:57.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.934 --> 00:03:00.534
Apparently, it's the first
Marvel movie with a love scene.

00:03:00.534 --> 00:03:02.133
[ Ohs and cheering ]

00:03:02.133 --> 00:03:03.567
It's a little awkward.

00:03:03.567 --> 00:03:05.100
Basically, the guy thinks
he's Iron Man,

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:06.801
only to find out he's Ant-Man.

00:03:06.801 --> 00:03:08.734
[ Laughter and ohs ]

00:03:08.734 --> 00:03:10.133
You know what I'm saying?

00:03:10.133 --> 00:03:11.934
-Oh.

00:03:11.934 --> 00:03:13.434
-Hey, I heard
about a Colorado man

00:03:13.434 --> 00:03:15.467
who set his mother's house
on fire

00:03:15.467 --> 00:03:18.200
while trying to get rid
of cobwebs with a blowtorch.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:20.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:22.100
When his mom said,
"Did he get the cobwebs?"

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:24.200
He was like,
"Technically, yes."

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:26.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.133 --> 00:03:28.234
And, finally,
a Southwest Airlines employee

00:03:28.234 --> 00:03:31.834
created a dress out of 800
lost luggage zipper pulls.

00:03:31.834 --> 00:03:33.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.167 --> 00:03:34.434
When she asks her husband
to zip her up,

00:03:34.434 --> 00:03:36.434
he finishes
about six hours later.

00:03:36.434 --> 00:03:38.901
Guys, the NASCAR Cup
Series Championship

00:03:38.901 --> 00:03:41.934
airs this Sunday,
right here on NBC,

00:03:41.934 --> 00:03:43.000
on your television!

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.801
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:03:44.801 --> 00:03:46.000
We love NASCAR.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.501
Now, at the end of the series,

00:03:47.501 --> 00:03:49.834
they give out an award
for Most Popular Driver,

00:03:49.834 --> 00:03:53.334
but they also give out
some other awards as well.

00:03:53.334 --> 00:03:54.467
I'll show you what I mean.
It's time for

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:55.834
"Tonight Show Superlatives."
Here we go.

00:03:55.834 --> 00:03:57.033
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:03:57.033 --> 00:03:58.501
